WEBVTT

00:01.350 --> 00:02.690
It is the present day.

00:03.370 --> 00:06.930
Fully-immersive games, in which
the users wear VR headsets

00:06.930 --> 00:10.340
to play as fully-realized
denizens of a fictional world...

00:13.070 --> 00:17.220
are dominating the gaming world.

00:19.740 --> 00:27.270
The pinnacle of these VR games,
boasting over 30 million players worldwide,

00:27.270 --> 00:29.130
is known as a god-tier game.

00:31.130 --> 00:33.130
Its name...

00:39.840 --> 00:42.100
is Shangri-La Frontier<i>!</i>

02:18.380 --> 02:20.150
Sky Clear!

02:20.150 --> 02:22.580
Crescent Vorpal!

02:29.030 --> 02:30.870
Go to sleep already...

02:31.130 --> 02:33.790
Wethermon the Tombguard!

02:49.750 --> 02:51.570
"It is as clear as a cloudless sky."

02:52.520 --> 02:57.980
Would you like to know the
truth of this world, son?

02:59.850 --> 03:03.560
I would be honored.

03:05.020 --> 03:09.120
Then there's a little something
I'd like you to do for me.

03:09.120 --> 03:13.580
Only an Ancient Craftsman can
fix up stuff from the Divinity.

03:13.580 --> 03:15.570
If there's no Ancient Craftsman around,

03:15.570 --> 03:18.560
I just need to turn Bilac
into an Ancient Craftsman!

03:20.390 --> 03:22.550
You got it, birdman.

03:23.180 --> 03:24.900
I'll play along.

03:25.310 --> 03:27.570
I'm gonna become an Ancient Craftsman!

03:27.570 --> 03:30.390
Yay, Big Sis Bee!

03:30.390 --> 03:32.110
Hell yeah!

03:32.110 --> 03:35.080
Let's start the plan to cultivate Bilac!

03:35.080 --> 03:36.220
Yes, indeed!

03:36.220 --> 03:38.100
Y-Yeah!

03:40.790 --> 03:46.380
Half-Naked Birdman and the Gang in Golem Paradise

03:42.330 --> 03:45.490
Lover of trash games,

03:45.490 --> 03:46.860
high-school student Rakuro Hizutome,

03:46.860 --> 03:49.450
AKA Sunraku, hurried on ahead.

03:47.380 --> 03:52.390
Rakuro Hizutome  Character: Sunraku

03:50.460 --> 03:53.870
In order to proceed in the game's story,

03:54.260 --> 03:56.620
he needed to acquire a magic operations unit,

03:57.030 --> 03:59.640
and make Bilac into an Ancient Craftsman.

04:03.180 --> 04:04.870
All right!

04:06.510 --> 04:09.640
Made it to the new area!

04:09.640 --> 04:12.010
Okay, enough of that!

04:12.390 --> 04:16.320
How long do I gotta stay stuffed
in there with Ignoramus?!

04:16.320 --> 04:19.800
Ah, my maiden's warmth grows distant!

04:19.800 --> 04:21.170
Freak.

04:21.170 --> 04:24.490
Fair enough. We'll probably
be swarmed by enemies soon,

04:24.490 --> 04:25.190
so I'll take this off.

04:25.190 --> 04:26.690
No! It's over already?

04:26.690 --> 04:28.070
What's over, huh?!

04:28.930 --> 04:31.750
Then may I return to my original form?

04:31.750 --> 04:34.200
Sure. No one's around to see you.

04:33.010 --> 04:34.200
Staring Bird Mask
equipped.

04:38.020 --> 04:40.460
But... this area...

04:40.460 --> 04:44.460
Ruins of Past Glories

04:44.460 --> 04:47.850
From a distance, it looked like
the bones of a living thing...

04:47.850 --> 04:50.230
but it's actually man-made, huh?

04:50.230 --> 04:52.700
It's enormous!

04:52.700 --> 04:55.920
It was made during the Divinity, I guess.

04:55.920 --> 04:57.840
Why'd they build this giant thing?

04:59.420 --> 05:02.600
And why'd their culture die out?

05:03.630 --> 05:05.860
Were they fighting something?

05:06.390 --> 05:07.740
Or...

05:07.740 --> 05:09.940
Seek out "Bahamut."

05:12.110 --> 05:13.450
Sunraku-san?

05:13.450 --> 05:15.450
Whoops, cut that out.

05:15.890 --> 05:21.000
Meeting the Professor guy from the
lore clan switched my lore brain on.

05:21.360 --> 05:26.960
Will you join us in exploring
the truth of this world?

05:27.680 --> 05:30.090
The truth of this world?

05:30.400 --> 05:31.610
Yes.

05:31.610 --> 05:34.930
To share what information we acquire,

05:34.930 --> 05:40.100
and bring the truths of the enigmatic
<i>Shangri-La Frontier</i> to light!

05:40.870 --> 05:44.480
This Professor guy's right about one thing...

05:45.130 --> 05:49.220
The scenario flags in Shangri-La Frontier <i>
are really specific and hard to unravel.</i>

05:49.780 --> 05:52.290
It's unlikely I could find them all out

05:52.290 --> 05:55.650
without a deeper understanding
of the world setting.

05:55.960 --> 05:56.990
In particular...

05:58.010 --> 06:02.330
The scenario flag for one of
the SLF<i> world's Seven Colossi,</i>

06:01.330 --> 06:02.330
Unique Monster
Lycagon the Nightslayer
Encountered

06:02.670 --> 06:06.530
Lycagon the Nightslayer...

06:11.720 --> 06:13.720
You've received a friend request
from the              . Accept?

06:11.720 --> 06:13.720
No

06:11.720 --> 06:13.720
Yes

06:11.720 --> 06:13.720
Professor

06:13.900 --> 06:15.840
Sunraku has been added
to your friend list.

06:15.230 --> 06:19.180
Can I assume you agree to my proposal, then?

06:19.540 --> 06:22.350
Yeah. I've just got a few
things to take care of, first.

06:22.970 --> 06:25.170
We'll have to start on this later.

06:26.560 --> 06:29.480
That said, if you wanna hear about Wethermon,

06:29.820 --> 06:32.170
there's someone who knows way more than me.

06:32.540 --> 06:34.510
Her name's Pencilgon.

06:35.290 --> 06:39.490
Pencilgon? The Giant Killer?

06:37.010 --> 06:40.100
Giant Killer

06:39.490 --> 06:44.000
I'd heard she was talking
to Schwarz Vulf, but...

06:40.540 --> 06:44.000
Schwarz Vulf

06:44.450 --> 06:46.340
Very well.

06:46.340 --> 06:51.070
Then, Sunraku-kun, let us meet again soon.

06:56.270 --> 07:00.730
Sheesh, I still can't square
that voice with that avatar.

07:02.410 --> 07:08.670
I'm sure glad he backed off when he
heard the name Pencilgon, though.

07:09.650 --> 07:14.910
Thanks for going under the bus to improve
my own game experience, Pencilgon!

07:15.360 --> 07:21.990
I wanna start messing with those guys
in the Inventoria as quick as I can!

07:23.130 --> 07:24.530
Hey, dope.

07:24.530 --> 07:29.200
We came <i>this</i> close to that professor
guy finding out about us, y'know?

07:29.520 --> 07:32.960
Nah, I'm pretty sure he knew I
was hiding something, at least.

07:33.540 --> 07:34.470
Impossible!

07:34.470 --> 07:39.510
The guy leads a lore clan.
He's not that dumb.

07:39.970 --> 07:44.480
I think he was just too polite to press
me on it during our first meeting.

07:45.100 --> 07:46.600
Anyway, forget all that!

07:47.310 --> 07:50.480
We finally reached the
area we were heading for!

07:50.480 --> 07:53.610
Time to shift gears and get looking
for that magic operations unit!

07:53.610 --> 07:55.110
Forward, ho!

07:55.110 --> 07:56.120
Hold on a sec.

07:56.120 --> 07:57.610
How come?

07:57.610 --> 08:01.200
I've been doin' a little
research on this area.

08:02.870 --> 08:04.520
Brilliant as ever, my fair maiden!

08:04.520 --> 08:09.240
The main thing to watch out for here
is a never-ending stream of golem—

08:21.110 --> 08:26.150
The whole place is swarming
with golems from the Divinity!

08:26.150 --> 08:27.640
Yeah, seems like it!

08:27.640 --> 08:29.270
There's one here right now!

08:29.270 --> 08:31.150
They're already here!

08:31.900 --> 08:35.040
Well, aren't you a big, tough-looking guy?

08:35.040 --> 08:37.150
Looks like a worker golem.

08:37.640 --> 08:40.240
All right, how to go about this?

08:52.390 --> 08:54.160
Fire attacks, huh?

08:54.160 --> 08:58.640
Looks like you've got power,
but no speed to go with it!

08:58.640 --> 09:00.560
We'll win this with speed!

09:00.560 --> 09:01.880
Follow me, Emul!

09:01.880 --> 09:03.140
Righty-o!

09:04.250 --> 09:06.580
Steel giant of the lost Divinity...

09:07.150 --> 09:10.060
Allow me to close the curtain
on your eternal wanderings!

09:11.150 --> 09:15.770
Sworvant Solo

09:11.690 --> 09:13.270
Sworvant Solo!

09:13.270 --> 09:15.030
Primal Slash!

09:13.270 --> 09:15.770
Primal Slash

09:17.530 --> 09:21.570
As long as I, the Wild Wind,
Aramiys am here...

09:19.420 --> 09:24.780
Wild Wind

09:21.960 --> 09:24.780
no enemy shall stand in our way!

09:26.800 --> 09:28.340
One hit, huh?

09:29.410 --> 09:31.540
Hey, hang on a minute, here!

09:31.910 --> 09:34.620
Did that fry all the item drops with it?!

09:35.020 --> 09:36.800
There's no loot here, man!

09:39.440 --> 09:41.050
I may have gotten a bit carried awa—

09:41.050 --> 09:42.490
You friggin' dope!

09:43.140 --> 09:48.950
Don't use a dragon-killer attack
to take out one little work golem!

09:49.450 --> 09:53.310
F-Fair maiden... not in the head, please!

09:53.310 --> 09:55.810
"Dragon-killer"?

09:56.400 --> 09:57.860
Aramiys.

09:57.860 --> 10:00.340
Kindly refrain from dropping damage
bombs like that, would you?

10:00.850 --> 10:02.320
Y-Yes, sir...

10:02.550 --> 10:05.940
Anyway, I get that Aramiys
is pretty OP and all,

10:05.940 --> 10:08.690
but these things don't seem
like that big a threat.

10:08.690 --> 10:10.080
Don't be stupid.

10:10.080 --> 10:13.710
Not all the golems here are gonna
be slowpokes like that one.

10:14.000 --> 10:17.090
The really scary golems are the
ones born from local elements.

10:17.380 --> 10:18.850
"Local elements"?

10:18.850 --> 10:22.020
You never know what they're
gonna pull on you.

10:27.570 --> 10:28.330
What the...

10:30.870 --> 10:31.480
This thing—

10:31.480 --> 10:32.890
Hold still, birdman!

10:42.020 --> 10:44.740
That was too freaking close!

10:46.410 --> 10:47.910
It blew itself up?!

10:48.300 --> 10:51.580
So that little ball was a
"local element" golem, huh?

10:51.580 --> 10:54.710
Like I said! You never know
what they're gonna pull!

10:55.020 --> 10:57.890
Sunraku-san! Look at that!

11:00.110 --> 11:05.050
Aramiys... I take back what I
said about the damage bombs.

11:11.820 --> 11:15.000
I think now's the time to really cut loose!

11:45.040 --> 11:47.580
Bilac! Careful about
triggering chain reactions!

11:47.580 --> 11:51.560
That thing keeps on spitting
out more Ball Golems!

11:51.840 --> 11:55.570
There's no point fighting the Ball
Golems if they'll just keep on coming.

11:56.260 --> 11:59.440
We've gotta get in close
and destroy the big body!

12:06.800 --> 12:08.360
Magic Edge!

12:12.820 --> 12:14.330
Sworvant Solo...

12:14.680 --> 12:16.120
Primal Slash!

12:24.170 --> 12:25.890
I've accomplished nothing.

12:25.890 --> 12:27.880
They just keep coming!

12:28.770 --> 12:32.940
Does it seem to you like they're
focused on Emul and Aramiys?

12:32.940 --> 12:35.890
Yeah, almost like it's got it out for them.

12:36.380 --> 12:42.400
It sees the high-level Aramiys and
caster-type Emul as the major threats, then?

12:42.900 --> 12:46.470
That's some pretty clever
AI you've got in there...

12:46.470 --> 12:47.780
But in that case...

12:48.670 --> 12:50.240
C'mon, Bilac!

12:50.240 --> 12:52.990
Now's our chance! Let's finish this thing!

12:53.620 --> 12:54.640
Got it!

12:55.870 --> 13:01.190
The Ball Golems aren't so thick around me,
so I can use my speed to get in close!

13:02.300 --> 13:03.380
Made it!

13:03.380 --> 13:06.270
Guess those smarts of yours
worked against you, huh?

13:06.270 --> 13:07.880
It's smashing time, Bilac!

13:07.880 --> 13:09.760
Right!

13:13.600 --> 13:14.870
What now?!

13:14.870 --> 13:18.350
I could make it with Moon Jumper
and Six-Boat Leap, but...

13:21.790 --> 13:22.750
Damn it!

13:23.440 --> 13:27.940
It's way too dangerous to mount an aerial
strike under bombardment like this!

13:28.920 --> 13:29.950
Sunraku-san!

13:29.950 --> 13:33.410
Too many balls! I can't go to help him!

13:33.410 --> 13:35.950
Get down, my lady's sister...

13:36.700 --> 13:38.140
Sworvant Solo!

13:38.140 --> 13:39.910
Primal Slash!

13:46.420 --> 13:47.900
That's our Swordsmaster!

13:47.900 --> 13:49.090
You saved my butt!

13:49.720 --> 13:54.590
I told you, my sword will cut down
all who stand in my lady's way!

13:59.410 --> 14:01.100
Darn it! It's running away again!

14:01.100 --> 14:04.100
I don't think it was in a
position to jump very far...

14:04.100 --> 14:07.320
This might be a good chance to
test out that little number!

14:08.340 --> 14:09.190
Marsh Daggers [V3]
Empire Bee Twinblades
Moonblade (Waxing)
Moonblade (Waning)

14:11.820 --> 14:12.610
Dropped Item
Dullahan General's Decapitator

14:16.450 --> 14:20.500
Let's show it the power
of the reborn Decapitator!

14:20.850 --> 14:22.160
Flame General's Decapitator
equipped.

14:22.820 --> 14:23.790
Skill...

14:25.170 --> 14:27.170
Glowing Pierce

14:25.190 --> 14:27.170
Glowing Pierce!

14:27.910 --> 14:30.480
If you're trying that hard
to avoid taking damage,

14:30.480 --> 14:33.380
you must not have much
in the way of vitality!

14:35.350 --> 14:36.300
The core!

14:36.720 --> 14:38.830
I think I like this newborn Decapitator!

14:38.830 --> 14:40.220
Leave the rest to me!

14:42.060 --> 14:44.230
Material Destroy

14:42.060 --> 14:44.610
Material Destroy!

14:49.820 --> 14:52.170
Eh? This might end... poorly.

14:52.510 --> 14:55.070
Everyone, retreat!

14:57.850 --> 14:59.240
Sunraku-san!

15:04.110 --> 15:07.980
I kinda had a feeling...
So the big one blows up, too?

15:07.980 --> 15:09.870
That was a close call.

15:09.870 --> 15:12.930
Fair maiden! I'm grateful for your safety!

15:12.930 --> 15:14.760
Sunraku-san!

15:17.060 --> 15:18.760
Something's coming down...

15:22.210 --> 15:24.170
An item drop, maybe?

15:24.170 --> 15:26.020
It's got an icon, so...

15:26.020 --> 15:31.270
Dropped Item
Blasting Earth Idol

15:26.850 --> 15:30.500
What's this? Kinda looks like
an egg with a dopey face...

15:30.500 --> 15:31.270
A haniwa?

15:32.060 --> 15:33.830
It's really rather cute!

15:33.830 --> 15:36.130
You really think so?

15:35.030 --> 15:51.880
Dropped Item
Blasting Earth Idol
A small-scale replica sometimes produced
from a naturally-spawning golem.
Produced by Cannonball Golems,
it unleashes a minor explosion
in response to a strong impact.

15:36.130 --> 15:39.360
Let's see... "Blasting Earth Idol."

15:39.360 --> 15:45.040
"A small-scale replica sometimes produced
from a naturally-spawning golem.

15:45.040 --> 15:48.350
Produced by Cannonball Golems,

15:48.350 --> 15:52.900
it unleashes a minor explosion
in response to a strong impact."

15:52.900 --> 15:56.730
"When the Blasting Earth Idol's
dance reaches its climax,

15:56.730 --> 15:59.510
it shoots flames from the earth..."

15:59.510 --> 16:02.510
Explosion? Hey, this thing is a grenade!

16:02.510 --> 16:05.770
It might've gone off if
you hadn't picked it up.

16:05.770 --> 16:08.900
Man, what a nasty parting gift.

16:09.290 --> 16:14.510
Let's toss it into the Inventoria and get
back to finding the magic operations unit!

16:20.810 --> 16:21.990
That felt like a good hit!

16:27.080 --> 16:28.370
Hell yeah!

16:28.370 --> 16:30.190
Brilliantly done!

16:36.770 --> 16:38.590
Another idol.

16:38.590 --> 16:42.600
Dropped Item
Sword-Denying Idol
Draws attention strongly
from certain monsters.
The more the Sword-Denying Idol
rejects them, the stronger
their interest becomes.

16:39.080 --> 16:42.600
A lady knight? It's pretty detailed.

16:42.990 --> 16:45.850
Draws attention from certain monsters, huh?

16:45.850 --> 16:48.860
Like goblins and orcs, maybe?

16:51.060 --> 16:53.480
I'm glad you're safe, my lady fair!

16:53.480 --> 16:55.990
Hands off, Ignoramus!

16:58.980 --> 17:01.280
Now the jaw?!

17:01.590 --> 17:04.720
Honestly, if the more it rejects them,
the more they like it...

17:04.720 --> 17:08.160
That sounds a little like Bilac and Aramiys.

17:08.430 --> 17:09.380
What is it?

17:09.380 --> 17:10.540
Nothing.

17:10.870 --> 17:13.500
Still, glad we've got this Decapitator.

17:13.910 --> 17:16.590
Due to the swords on the
outside of their bodies,

17:16.590 --> 17:19.550
my other weapons wouldn't
have reached the core.

17:19.960 --> 17:22.330
The high durability's a good thing, too!

17:23.720 --> 17:26.810
You bet it is. I reinforced
it myself, after all.

17:27.110 --> 17:31.620
Still, my job is a twinblade mercenary.

17:31.620 --> 17:34.780
It's easy to learn twinblade
and dagger-based skills.

17:34.780 --> 17:37.440
Longsword skills, not so much.

17:37.880 --> 17:41.610
It might be good practice
for wielding the Twin Moon,

17:41.610 --> 17:44.200
but I'll stick to twinblades
for the most part.

17:44.200 --> 17:49.830
Sunraku

17:45.610 --> 17:49.830
We managed to beat the golems
clustered around here.

17:50.520 --> 17:54.500
You really think the workshop
we're after is nearby?

17:54.500 --> 17:57.340
With the... marjik oppleration zoonit.

17:57.340 --> 17:59.670
Well, I can't really be sure.

17:59.670 --> 18:03.710
But since it's from the age of the Divinity,

18:03.710 --> 18:06.410
what we're looking for is
probably less like a forge,

18:06.410 --> 18:07.970
and more like a factory.

18:08.250 --> 18:10.110
A factory?

18:10.110 --> 18:15.310
A workshop where they're using
science to build things in secret

18:15.310 --> 18:17.520
was probably considered
a pretty important place.

18:18.120 --> 18:21.900
And if these ruins are the
result of an enemy attack,

18:21.900 --> 18:25.540
to keep it safe they'd probably
have put it wherever the security

18:25.540 --> 18:27.170
and defense golems are the thickest.

18:27.170 --> 18:32.510
Of course! Thus, you sought out the
place where the golems most thrived!

18:32.510 --> 18:34.770
What a smart idea, Sunraku-san!

18:34.770 --> 18:38.590
But I don't see any buildings that
look like what you're talking about.

18:38.590 --> 18:40.810
It's all rubble.

18:42.650 --> 18:45.050
Sunraku

18:45.370 --> 18:47.180
I'll bet it's somewhere around here.

18:49.090 --> 18:55.520
What kind of place is easiest to
protect from external threats?

18:59.850 --> 19:01.580
Somewhere underground!

19:01.580 --> 19:04.240
Sunraku-san, incredible!

19:08.690 --> 19:10.730
I can't see the bottom.

19:10.730 --> 19:12.330
Well yeah, birds can't see in the dark.

19:12.330 --> 19:14.160
It's just a mask!

19:14.580 --> 19:19.030
Now, my lady, regarding my
invitation to Cazzeria...

19:16.760 --> 19:19.030
There we are.

19:19.030 --> 19:21.520
Huh? I already turned you down.

19:19.030 --> 19:21.520
Had a feeling I'd find him here.

19:21.520 --> 19:22.920
That birdbrain.

19:21.520 --> 19:23.490
But why?!

19:23.490 --> 19:25.840
It's a simple walk away!

19:23.910 --> 19:30.470
He thought he could get away
with ignoring my email, did he?

19:25.840 --> 19:29.300
Hey, Cazzeria is home to
the Cait Siths, right?

19:29.300 --> 19:31.360
Yes indeed, birdman!

19:32.000 --> 19:35.620
Cazzeria is ally to Rabituza, a strong
empire across a blazing-hot desert!

19:32.410 --> 19:33.930
What do we do?

19:34.150 --> 19:37.670
I think he could use a little PKing, don't you?

19:35.620 --> 19:37.940
Sounds interesting, but Bilac's making
a face like she's not into it.

19:37.670 --> 19:39.800
Sounds good to me!

19:37.940 --> 19:39.800
It's just not my speed.

21:12.950 --> 21:20.210
SLF Mini

21:13.680 --> 21:17.530
SLF Theater!

21:16.770 --> 21:20.210
#31 Fortune Teller Rock Roll

21:17.530 --> 21:19.020
Mini!

21:20.210 --> 23:46.360
SLF Theater

21:22.380 --> 21:23.800
Hello, Mana-sa—

21:23.800 --> 21:25.690
Come, my lost lamb.

21:25.690 --> 21:29.550
Welcome to the fortune
telling house, Rock Roll.

21:30.490 --> 21:32.370
Have a seat.

21:32.370 --> 21:35.140
Ah... What is all this?

21:35.140 --> 21:37.040
Have a <i>seat</i>.

21:37.040 --> 21:38.710
R-Right...

21:41.380 --> 21:43.860
Crystal Ball (160mm, base emits light)
Packaged extra from a certain otome game

21:45.630 --> 21:54.500
Iwamaki Mana  Hobby: Otome Games

21:48.790 --> 21:54.500
My lost lamb. You are in love... aren't you?

21:55.440 --> 21:58.820
Um... Yes.

21:58.820 --> 22:01.880
Yet your love has not yet borne fruit.

22:01.880 --> 22:04.760
Well... Yes.

22:04.760 --> 22:07.110
Guess you haven't been aggressive enough.

22:07.110 --> 22:12.220
Um... shouldn't you be maintaining
the fortune teller act?

22:13.760 --> 22:18.100
The crystal shall tell
of your romantic destiny.

22:18.100 --> 22:20.520
I paid 20,000 yen for the special
edition it came with, after all.

22:20.520 --> 22:21.860
Right...

22:23.120 --> 22:25.860
I see it. I see it!

22:26.080 --> 22:28.860
A new game release that went
on sale two days ago...

22:28.860 --> 22:33.620
A game on which opinions of whether it's a
good or trash game are passionately split...

22:36.110 --> 22:41.920
He's a physical media guy, so if he hasn't
bought it here, he doesn't have it.

22:42.300 --> 22:44.790
In other words, he'll be coming by to get it.

22:47.300 --> 22:49.100
Heya.

22:49.100 --> 22:51.180
Iwamaki-san, got any new stuff in?

22:51.180 --> 22:52.960
Well...

22:52.960 --> 22:54.770
Huh? Was someone just here?

22:55.110 --> 22:57.760
A kamaitachi, perhaps.

22:58.520 --> 23:01.190
Now. You're after this, aren't you?

23:02.900 --> 23:05.720
Yeah, this one smells like a real stinker!

23:05.720 --> 23:10.010
All the positive online
reviews totally reek of copy-paste...

23:10.010 --> 23:12.570
<i>Superfun Fantasy</i>!

23:12.570 --> 23:15.070
I can't believe you were
brave enough to stock this!

23:15.930 --> 23:19.410
Well, I knew I'd sell at least two...

23:20.890 --> 23:22.990
Thank you for coming!

23:28.040 --> 23:30.590
Now, my lost lamb...

23:30.590 --> 23:32.590
I'll knock 10% off the price just for you.

23:32.590 --> 23:34.760
It has an online mode.

23:34.760 --> 23:36.470
I-I'll take it.

23:37.640 --> 23:39.620
Thank you for coming!

23:42.170 --> 23:44.930
Rei-chan's got the "chase" part down...
